  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Question cards are available, and a volunteer can hold short discussion pauses in a room.\", \"decision\": \"How should visitors collect questions for a volunteer?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVisitors hand question cards to the volunteer during the visit, and the next pause addresses them in arrival order. Questions retain a visible sequence without stopping every viewing moment.\nVisitors write question cards before the discussion pause, and the volunteer groups similar questions. The pause can address shared concerns together.\nThe volunteer starts the discussion pause with a question and invites visitors to add question cards. An opening exchange helps visitors decide what they want to ask."
    }
